      <workList xml:id="workDesc_770b4245">
         <work xml:id="work_id04989c21">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_73e90305">C3:001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_idff2a3c3a" xml:lang="de">Anekdoten eines reisenden Russen über die Staatsverfassung, Sitten und Gebräuche der Dänen</title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_679dcb3b" xml:lang="da">En reisende Russers Anekdoter over de Danskes Statsforfatning, Sæder og Skikke, i Breve til sine Venner</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_4d689a79"/>
            <creation xml:id="creation_idbb0b1acb">
               <date isodate="1771" xml:id="date_68b0141b">1771</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id53c9c1df">
               <p xml:id="idm232">In September 1770 the minister and the de facto regent <persName xml:id="idm233" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Friedrich Struensee</persName> signed the abolition of censorship – an act that drew international attention and was commented upon all over Europe at the time, even enticing Voltaire to praise the decision. In Denmark the newly gained freedom of press led to the publication of a wide array of various pamphlets, and in 1771 Scheibe published his <rend xml:id="idm234" fontstyle="italic">Anekdoten eines reisenden Russen</rend>. In order to clad his serious criticism of Denmark – the government’s overspending, the country’s customs and the people’s national character – in a satirical tone he employed the popular framework based on a foreigner’s travel diary and letters. The pamphlet created somewhat of a stir among intellectuals and prompted many responses: <rend xml:id="idm235" fontstyle="italic">Velmeent Svar til den Russiske Bagtalere. Af Sandheds-Elskere</rend> (Copenhagen, 1771); <rend xml:id="idm236" fontstyle="italic">En døbt Jødes alvorlige og skiemtefulde Giensvar til den som nylig har ladet udgive det Skrift: Velmeent Svar til den Russiske Bagtalere</rend> (Copenhagen, 1771); <rend xml:id="idm237" fontstyle="italic">Breve fra en Dansk til Forfatteren af en foregiven reisende Russers Anekdoter</rend> (Copenhagen, 1771); <rend xml:id="idm238" fontstyle="italic">Sendschreiben eines Russen aus St. Petersburg an den Russen aus Deutschland der Dänische Anecdoten zum Gebrauch der Gewürzkrämer sammlet</rend> (Copenhagen, 1771); <rend xml:id="idm239" fontstyle="italic">Den vildfarende Russers Veyviiser, anstillet i nogle Breve til Ham selv</rend> (Copenhagen, 1771); and <persName xml:id="idm240" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johan Carl Frederik Hellfried</persName>’s <rend xml:id="idm241" fontstyle="italic">Briefe eines Dänen an den Verfasser der Anecdoten eines angeblichen reisenden Russen</rend> (Copenhagen, 1771). Scheibe’s <rend xml:id="idm242" fontstyle="italic">Anekdoten</rend> was revised and improved several times within the first year and appeared first in a German and later in a Danish translation. Scheibe's German pamphlet received an extensive review in <rend xml:id="idm243" fontstyle="italic">Kiøbenhavns </rend>
                  <rend xml:id="idm244" fontstyle="italic">Adresse-Contoirs kritiske Journal</rend> in 1771, which concludes that 'when reviewing these letters, they betray without difficulty a man of taste and insight, but also of great volatility in judgement, and a desire to make all the little things a flaw of national character; this seems to be more an effect of displeasure with certain people rather than having a discreet and mature authority [...] There is no doubt that he is a German, though his language in no way is tasteful, and his style is in many places very careless' (col. 183). The rescript concerning censorship did not have the intended effect and was therefore revised in 1771. It was abolished completely the following year when Struensee was beheaded.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_58959cef">
